Now we need to unload payload to get origin_availability_confirmed and origin_node_ready true while keeping origin_node_occupied true and origin_availability_locked true. Use unload_origin_payload: precondition requires candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (true), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (true), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (true), origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha (true), origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha (true), not origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha (currently false). Effect: origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha true, origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha true, cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha true, not origin_payload_linked origin_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha (removes link). Note origin_node_occupied remains true (not in effect). origin_availability_locked remains true (not in effect). Good.

Now we have origin node occupied, ready, locked, confirmed, cargo available again.

Now we need to lock origin availability? Actually after load/unload we already have origin_availability_locked true and origin_availability_confirmed true (from unload). So we don't need lock_origin_availability action (which would also set them but requires not locked). So we can skip lock.

Now we need to do similar for destination_availability_alpha.

Steps for destination:

- Attach task profile to destination_availability_alpha: attach_task_profile ?candidate destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (needs candidate_created destination_availability_alpha (true), vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (currently false). So we need to allocate a vehicle unit to destination_availability_alpha first. We have vehicle_unit_beta available initially. Let's allocate vehicle_unit_beta to destination_availability_alpha.

Action allocate_vehicle_unit ?candidate destination_availability_alpha ?vehicle_unit_beta. Precondition: candidate_created destination_availability_alpha (true), not vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (true), vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta (true). Effect: vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha true, candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta true, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta becomes false.

Now attach task profile: attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha.

Now confirm preparedness: confirm_candidate_preparedness destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha.

Now activate destination node: activate_destination_node destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha.

Now load destination payload: load_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha. Precondition: candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha (true after confirm), destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha (true), cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha (true after origin unload), not destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha (currently false). Effect: destination_node_occupied destination_node_alpha true, destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha true, destination_payload_linked destination_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha true, cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha false.

Now unload destination payload: unload_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha. Precondition: candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha (true), candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (true), destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha (true), destination_node_occupied destination_node_alpha (true), destination_payload_linked destination_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha (true), not destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha (false). Effect: destination_node_ready destination_node_alpha true, destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha true, cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha true, not destination_payload_linked destination_availability_alpha cargo_payload_alpha (removes link). destination_availability_locked stays true, destination_node_occupied stays true.

Now we have destination node occupied, ready, locked, confirmed, cargo available again.

Now we need to assemble transport leg. Preconditions for assemble_transport_leg:

- origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha (true)
- destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha (true)
- origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (true)
- destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha (true)
- origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha (true after unload)
- destination_node_ready destination_node_alpha (true after unload)
- origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha (true)
- destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha (true)
- transport_leg_available transport_leg_alpha (true initially)

Thus we can assemble.

Action: assemble_transport_leg origin_availability_alpha destination_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha destination_node_alpha transport_leg_alpha.

Effect: transport_leg_assembled transport_leg_alpha true, transport_leg_origin_linked transport_leg_alpha origin_node_alpha true, transport_leg_destination_linked transport_leg_alpha destination_node_alpha true, transport_leg_available false.

Now we need transport_leg_loading_authorized: action authorize_transport_leg_loading ?transport_leg transport_leg_alpha ?origin_availability origin_availability_alpha ?route_task_profile route_task_profile_alpha. Precondition: transport_leg_assembled transport_leg_alpha (true), origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha (true), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (true), not transport_leg_loading_authorized transport_leg_alpha (true). Effect: transport_leg_loading_authorized transport_leg_alpha true.

Now we need to load container onto leg for shift_candidate_beta. Preconditions for load_container_onto_leg: ?candidate - schedule_candidate (shift_candidate_beta), ?loading_container loading_container_beta, ?transport_leg transport_leg_alpha.

Precondition: candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta (need to prepare), candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_beta transport_leg_alpha (we have from init? Yes init has candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_beta transport_leg_alpha true), candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta (true from init), loading_container_available loading_container_beta (currently true? We haven't used loading_container_beta yet; it's available initially), transport_leg_assembled transport_leg_alpha (true after assemble), transport_leg_loading_authorized transport_leg_alpha (true after authorize), not loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta (currently false). Effect: loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta true, loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha true, loading_container_available loading_container_beta false.

Thus we need shift_candidate_beta prepared, and also need candidate_loading_container_linked (already true). Good.

Now we need to prepare shift_candidate_beta: need candidate_created (true), vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta (need to allocate a vehicle unit), candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (need to attach), then confirm preparedness.

We also need candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha (goal). We'll assign operator after preparing.

We need candidate_skill_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta skill_certificate_alpha (goal). Assign skill certificate after prepared.

We need candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha (goal). Assign compliance certificate after prepared.

We need candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_beta (goal). This can be achieved via one of the establish_clearance_* actions. They require candidate_loading_verified ?candidate, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, and depending on leg loaded states (origin_leg_loaded/destination_leg_loaded). Goal does not require origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded. We have loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha true after loading container. We need loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta true (goal). We'll have that after load_container_onto_leg.

We need candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta (goal). That's a precondition for establish_clearance_* actions. So we need to verify loading profile first.

We need candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta (goal). This is a precondition for verify_loading_profile actions. So we need to stage candidate.

Thus sequence for shift_candidate_beta:

- Prepare shift_candidate_beta (vehicle allocated, task profile linked, confirm preparedness).
- Assign operator (after releasing from alpha).
- Assign skill certificate.
- Assign compliance certificate.
- Reserve equipment resource? Not required in goal but may be needed for staging? Actually stage_schedule_candidate requires candidate_prepared, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, candidate_task_profile_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading. So we need loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked (we will have after loading container onto leg). Also need candidate_task_profile_linked (we will have). Also need not origin_leg_loaded (we haven't loaded origin leg; origin_leg_loaded is false unless we performed assemble_origin_loaded_leg etc. We haven't done that, so origin_leg_loaded false). Good.

Thus after we load container onto leg (loading_container_loaded true, loading_container_leg_linked true), we can stage schedule candidate.

- Stage schedule candidate: stage_schedule_candidate shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha route_task_profile_alpha. Precondition: candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta (true after preparation), candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta (true), loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta (true after load), loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha (true after load), candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (true), not origin_leg_loaded transport_leg_alpha (we need to ensure origin_leg_loaded false), not candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta (true). Effect: candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta true.

Now we need to verify loading profile to get candidate_loading_verified. We can use either verify_loading_profile_destination_flag (requires destination_leg_loaded) or verify_loading_profile_nominal (requires not destination_leg_loaded). We have not loaded destination leg (destination_leg_loaded false). So we can use verify_loading_profile_nominal. Precondition: candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta (true), candidate_skill_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta skill_certificate_alpha (need to have assigned), candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha (need assigned), candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta (true), loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha (true), destination_leg_loaded transport_leg_alpha (false), not candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta (true). Effect: candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta true.

Thus we need to assign skill certificate and operator before verification.

Now after loading verified, we can establish clearance. Which establish_clearance action to use? Since we have loading_container_leg_linked true, loading_container_loaded true, and we have not origin_leg_loaded and not destination_leg_loaded (we haven't set those). So we can use establish_clearance_nominal (requires candidate_loading_verified, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_clearance_established). Effect: candidate_clearance_established true and route_sequence_context_set true.

Thus after verification, we can execute establish_clearance_nominal shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha.

Now we need candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (we will attach earlier).

Now we need candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha (assign operator after preparing and after releasing operator from alpha). We'll need to release operator from shift_candidate_alpha after achieving operator_alignment_confirmed.

Now we need operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha (goal). This requires constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha and candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_alpha driver_operator_alpha. So we need to apply operational constraint to shift_candidate_alpha first, then confirm operator alignment.

We also need constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha (goal). Action apply_operational_constraint requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha (true from init), candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (true from init), operational_constraint_available operational_constraint_alpha (true init), candidate_operational_constraint_linked shift_candidate_alpha operational_constraint_alpha (true init), not constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha (true initially). Effect: constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha true, and not operational_constraint_available operational_constraint_alpha (makes it unavailable). Good.

After that, we can confirm operator alignment: confirm_operator_alignment shift_candidate_alpha driver_operator_alpha. Precondition: constraint_applied shift_candidate_alpha (now true), candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_alpha driver_operator_alpha (true from init), not operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha (true). Effect: operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha true.

